The Hailstone Tragedy of Lothar Collatz.

Romeo, a restless number who rises and falls.
Juliet, a patient lady who knows only how to halve and to treble.


                    Act I: The only act.

                    Scene I: A question of parity.

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Juliet:
  Listen to your heart!
  Is the remainder of the quotient between you and a big cat as good as nothing?

Romeo:
  If so, let us proceed to scene III.

                    Scene II: Romeo is odd.

Juliet:
  You are the sum of the product of the sum of a big cat and a cat and yourself and a cat!
  Open your heart!

Romeo:
  Let us proceed to scene IV.

                    Scene III: Romeo is even.

Juliet:
  You are the quotient between yourself and a big cat!
  Open your heart!

                    Scene IV: Exeunt.

[Exeunt]
